Defer the XrdpIme engine switch on reconnect until Unicode input arrives.

Local change on top of xrdp-0.10.6.1-ibus-unicode.patch (not upstream).
The first viewer connection already switched lazily, on the first Unicode
character; a reconnect switched immediately for the whole viewer session.
Scancode-only clients (for example Jump Desktop with a physical keyboard)
then reached XrdpIme, which passes every key through, so a remote pinyin
engine could never be used. Reconnects now behave like the first connection.
The previous engine is still recorded on the first Unicode character and
restored on viewer disconnect.

--- a/sesman/chansrv/input_ibus.c
+++ b/sesman/chansrv/input_ibus.c
@@ -376,8 +376,11 @@
 
     if (bus)
     {
-        /* Already initialized, just re-enable it */
-        return xrdp_input_enable();
+        /* Already initialized. Like the first connection, defer switching the
+         * global engine to XrdpIme until the first Unicode character arrives,
+         * so a viewer that only sends scancodes keeps the user's own engine
+         * (for example a remote pinyin engine). */
+        return 0;
     }
 
     /* Wait because the ibus daemon may not be ready on first login */
